Controller calls -> Service, uses the -> Repo interface, executes queries via JPA -> Database, returns rows as entities

Repository
    - Prefer interfaces and let Spring Data JPA provide the implementation
    - Single responsibility, one repo per aggregate/entity

Service
    - Focus on single business concern

Controller
    - Root package for all REST controllers. Organized by feature/domain.

Configuration
    - Application configuration files
    - Integration settings
    - properties, datasource, security (securityConfig), web, app
    - centralized, callable by all the layers

    - group config by concern ^
    - Profile, based setup
    - @Configuration and @Bean
    - @Validated, validate properties
    - config only wires components

Exception
    - Custom exceptions used across the application, handled consistently through a global handler
    - base, business, system, validation

